1
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:36,020
Mokku and Grandpa's life together was very happy.

2
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:50,020
But because Grandpa doted only on Mokku, Red Beard, a mouse who had lived there first, grew jealous. He lured in the wicked fox Kenken and threw Mokku into the river.

3
00:01:55,679 --> 00:02:03,080
Fortunately, Mokku was saved by the Oak Tree Fairy, but Red Beard didn't give up, waiting for another chance to finish Mokku off.

4
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:23,180
Mokku!

5
00:02:28,569 --> 00:02:29,569
Where am I?

6
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:31,220
Mokku, how's your fever?

7
00:02:31,989 --> 00:02:34,940
Ah, it's gone down. You'll be all right now.

8
00:02:35,315 --> 00:02:37,260
Grandpa cured me, didn't he?

9
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:43,860
Grandpa prayed to God to save you, even if it cost his own life.

10
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:47,200
If you aren't grateful to Grandpa, you'll be punished, Mokku.

11
00:02:49,290 --> 00:02:52,260
I'm sorry for worrying you, Grandpa.

12
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:21,820
Really, Peeko? Congratulations!

13
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:22,500
Mokku!

14
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:23,160
What is it?

15
00:03:23,644 --> 00:03:25,780
What are you talking to Peeko about?

16
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:29,360
Can't you hear her, Grandpa?

17
00:03:29,765 --> 00:03:33,060
Look, she's saying her babies were born!

18
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:42,420
Oho, babies? Well, congratulations, Peeko.

19
00:03:42,864 --> 00:03:45,500
Two boys and two girls, they say.

20
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,780
I bet the babies are so cute.

21
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:05,980
Well of course they're cute! Even to me, Mokku, you're just as precious.

22
00:04:08,330 --> 00:04:10,140
Pika, hurry up and bring them here!

23
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:19,100
They said, "Mokku is a troublemaker, so we don't want them playing together." Who do they think they are?!

24
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:24,220
See, that's what won't do.

25
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:26,940
You mustn't do mean things or bully your friends.

26
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:29,140
You have to get along with them, no matter what.

27
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:30,260
Yeah.

28
00:04:30,469 --> 00:04:34,000
I know. If I don't, I won't be able to become human, right?

29
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:36,740
Huh? Mokku, become human?

30
00:04:37,105 --> 00:04:42,320
Yes, exactly. You'll never become human unless you're a good boy. You could never become one. Now then...

31
00:04:42,470 --> 00:04:45,960
I'll become kindhearted and turn into a human soon.

32
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,500
Look.

33
00:04:48,725 --> 00:04:50,760
I can even fold my nightclothes neatly.

34
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:59,940
A wooden puppet made of dead wood becoming human?

35
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:03,140
As if such a ridiculous thing could happen.

36
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,700
Even with all my skill, that would be a bit impossible.

37
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:19,480
Damn brat! It's irritating enough that a puppet can move and talk, and now he wants to become a real human?!

38
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,520
You'd better quit getting so full of yourself!

39
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:39,180
And what does that old man see in a cheeky puppet bastard like him anyway?!

40
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:48,480
Listen. Hate to brag, but with my build, my face, and this long tail, I'm way better-looking.

41
00:05:53,840 --> 00:06:00,660
Just you wait. I'll crunch him to splinters with these sharp fangs of mine!

42
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,900
Hurry, hurry! Hurry, hurry!

43
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,660
Sorry to keep you waiting!

44
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,840
Wait!

45
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:16,500
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

46
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,520
Don't scare me like that!

47
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:18,180
Hold it!

48
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,200
Stop!

49
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:33,320
It's all right now, Big Brother.

50
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:39,560
You idiot, you clumsy fool, you blockhead, you bungler, you moron!

51
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:45,680
Look, just because you're educated, Big Brother, did you really have to rattle off every insult in the book?

52
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:52,760
Hmph, so what?! If you hadn't sneezed back then, we could've stolen the chicken from that bird shop!

53
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:58,660
But that was because you let one rip, wasn't it? It smelled so pungent, I couldn't help myself!

54
00:06:58,969 --> 00:07:01,140
Nature calls, so what was I supposed to do?!

55
00:07:02,090 --> 00:07:06,600
Don't make me yell. My stomach is sticking to my back already, damn it.

56
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:19,940
Even his head is made of oak right through.

57
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:27,180
He acts just like a child.

58
00:07:29,290 --> 00:07:31,860
And yet, and yet...

59
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:37,900
When he's lonely... Well, well, that's the smell of sandwiches!

60
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:40,900
I smell ham, cheese, and corned beef too!

61
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,400
I wonder why, Pero.

62
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:45,740
Go swipe that lunch.

63
00:07:46,005 --> 00:07:49,260
But Mokku hasn't forgotten being thrown into the river yet.

64
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,880
Just blame that on the rat.

65
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,840
He's the one who pushed him in, after all.

66
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,420
That's not fair...

67
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:57,240
Boss Kenken.

68
00:07:57,615 --> 00:08:03,800
Oh, Akashi... Look, what I mean is, I'm truly planning to beat Mokku up for your sake.

69
00:08:05,450 --> 00:08:06,840
Really?

70
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:10,900
Do my eyes look like they're lying? Huh? Well? Take a look!

71
00:08:13,135 --> 00:08:15,380
Boss, you've got crust in your eye.

72
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:20,100
Idiot! Mokku's getting away!

73
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,680
Leave it to me!

74
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:37,559
Next Episode

75
00:08:37,759 --> 00:08:44,159
Huh? Oh, Mokku... Good morning to you.

76
00:08:44,405 --> 00:08:45,920
It's a weasel's remains.

77
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:54,080
Just wait up, Mokku! Hey, hey, did you know they opened a super fun game arcade in town?

78
00:08:54,569 --> 00:09:01,560
You can't trust anything Kenken or Hanaguro say. Mokku, are you talking about the time you got pushed into the creek?

79
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:04,180
Red Beard the rat did that, you know.

80
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:05,540
I wonder why?

81
00:09:06,655 --> 00:09:07,740
Red Beard did?

82
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:11,220
It pisses him off that your grandfather dotes on you.

83
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,500
I wonder why?

84
00:09:13,255 --> 00:09:15,800
I've never been mean to Red Beard.

85
00:09:15,950 --> 00:09:17,880
That's just the kind of guy he is.

86
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:20,980
If you want to be a good boy, you have to hang out with good friends.

87
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:25,760
Like us... Wait, that doesn't sound right!

88
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:31,520
Exactly, exactly. Why don't you hang out with us—er, with us, Mokku? Huh?

89
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:33,240
But I have to go to school.

90
00:09:33,725 --> 00:09:35,980
Listen, Mokku. At the arcade...

91
00:09:36,165 --> 00:09:39,840
...there's even a machine that shoots out gold and silver coins for just one copper coin!

92
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:41,700
What? Gold and silver coins?

93
00:09:43,239 --> 00:09:50,960
Grandfather is the poorest guy in the village, right? He'd be thrilled if you brought some money home. Hey, Mokku, why is that, anyway?

94
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:56,360
But I don't have any money... Well, we could lend you some...

95
00:10:00,569 --> 00:10:01,900
Will you really lend it to me?

96
00:10:04,419 --> 00:10:06,640
Mokku, don't give in to temptation!

97
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,280
You again?!

98
00:10:08,645 --> 00:10:11,480
Go straight to school! Don't you want to become human?!

99
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:13,140
Shut up, Mokku!

100
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:18,580
Hey, Mokku. Just who do you think you're talking to?

101
00:10:19,070 --> 00:10:20,280
The Cricket... Huh?

102
00:10:21,109 --> 00:10:22,280
Huh? A cricket?

103
00:10:22,725 --> 00:10:25,080
N-No, nobody!

104
00:10:27,604 --> 00:10:30,960
What's in Kenken's bag are beer bottle caps!

105
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,000
I'm telling you, they're not copper!

106
00:10:33,001 --> 00:10:44,880
Pleased to meet you. I'm hungry, so I'm going to school. I want your lunch.

107
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:48,640
Your lunch has arrived.

108
00:10:50,869 --> 00:10:51,869
My lunch has arrived.

109
00:10:52,999 --> 00:10:55,480
My lunch has arrived.

110
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:58,420
Not yet.

111
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:11,060
This is the lunch Grandpa made specially for me!

112
00:11:11,405 --> 00:11:12,405
Like hell I'll let you take it!

113
00:11:16,285 --> 00:11:17,285
Mokkun!

114
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,140
Mokkun!

115
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:28,040
Mokkun!

116
00:11:28,041 --> 00:11:29,041
Mokkun!

117
00:11:35,859 --> 00:11:44,580
Like I'll let you get away two days in a row!

118
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:48,020
Just because Grandfather dotes on you doesn't make you lucky.

119
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,620
I wonder why?

120
00:12:58,780 --> 00:12:59,780
(Pokemon)

121
00:13:01,059 --> 00:13:02,140
Ha-ha-ha!

122
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:03,380
(Pokemon)

123
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:11,200
Where am I...?

124
00:13:16,179 --> 00:13:28,480
I fell from so high up, but nothing's broken! That's a puppet made by Grandpa for you. Ah, Grandpa must be worried...

125
00:13:29,079 --> 00:13:31,820
I have to get back soon...

126
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:37,060
Being all alone is so lonely... I know! I'll sing a song as I go!

127
00:13:42,129 --> 00:13:48,220
Cricket is my friend,

128
00:13:50,029 --> 00:13:56,560
We're the very best of pals.

129
00:13:57,220 --> 00:14:00,320
Even so, even so,

130
00:14:01,929 --> 00:14:04,420
Even though he's a ghost,

131
00:14:06,199 --> 00:14:09,560
He comes out in broad daylight to lecture me!

132
00:14:09,734 --> 00:14:15,740
What a total busybody!

133
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:19,160
Hey, that's not fair, Mokku!

134
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:29,540
Such a meddlesome busybody!

135
00:14:31,789 --> 00:14:33,700
What's that supposed to mean?! Calling me a busybody!

136
00:14:34,910 --> 00:14:36,120
Hmph, suit yourself!

137
00:14:36,121 --> 00:14:39,100
(Laughter)

138
00:14:45,289 --> 00:14:47,120
I'm scared...

139
00:14:52,569 --> 00:14:54,300
*sigh*

140
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:11,300
"Grandpa, good morning." "Good morning." "Grandpa, help me." "G-Good morning."

141
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,360
Aaaaaah!

142
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:18,420
You bastards!

143
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,200
(Burst of laughter)

144
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:28,620
The brat's completely fine?

145
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:31,460
Ah, he's surprisingly tough. Wonder why?

146
00:15:32,135 --> 00:15:37,160
This is our perfect chance to get rid of him. Are we just going to wait around for him to drop dead?

147
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,880
There's a woodcutter's shack deep in the forest. Lure him inside!

148
00:15:41,079 --> 00:15:44,740
He's frightened out of his mind. This is our chance.

149
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,400
Oh, Redbeard!

150
00:16:02,590 --> 00:16:06,540
Mokku, I looked all over for you. Thank goodness.

151
00:16:06,820 --> 00:16:09,320
Were you worried about me, Redbeard?

152
00:16:10,750 --> 00:16:16,260
You're Grandpa's favorite, after all. If anything happened to you, it'd break his heart.

153
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:24,340
Thanks, Redbeard. To be honest, I completely misunderstood you before. I thought you were in with Kenken and Hanaguro. I'm sorry.

154
00:16:26,059 --> 00:16:31,460
I tried to get your lunchbox back from that Kenken, but I couldn't. I'm sorry.

155
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:36,280
Thank you. You really are my friend after all.

156
00:16:40,529 --> 00:16:44,700
There's a woodcutter's shack right over there. Let's rest a bit.

157
00:16:45,389 --> 00:16:52,540
But if I don't get home soon, Grandpa will... / Look, your jacket and pants are soaking wet. If you don't dry them off before going home, you'll get scolded.

158
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:54,740
Yeah.

159
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:18,020
[[MUSIC]]

160
00:17:22,394 --> 00:17:26,640
Looks like there's a bird's nest. Might be in the attic.

161
00:17:27,599 --> 00:17:28,600
The attic?

162
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Yeah.

163
00:17:36,699 --> 00:17:44,060
Why don't you go take a look, Mokku? I'll gather firewood in the meantime. / Okay, I'll go see. I bet they're adorable.

164
00:17:46,589 --> 00:17:49,240
Be careful, Mokku. Don't fall.

165
00:17:49,495 --> 00:17:50,880
Thanks!

166
00:18:06,779 --> 00:18:08,700
Oh! It's Peeko and Pico!

167
00:18:09,029 --> 00:18:10,360
Ah! Mokku!

168
00:18:24,499 --> 00:18:27,260
Is this your baby? How cute!

169
00:18:27,261 --> 00:18:34,740
(Fast-forwarding)

170
00:18:38,459 --> 00:18:39,660
(Fast-forwarding)

171
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:42,440
(Fast-forwarding)

172
00:18:54,259 --> 00:18:56,260
(Fast-forwarding)

173
00:18:56,709 --> 00:18:58,100
The ladder is gone!

174
00:19:11,249 --> 00:19:15,600
Wood is helpless against fire. This ought to turn that bastard to ash.

175
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:31,340
(Dog yelping)

176
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:36,260
(Dog yelping)

177
00:19:41,304 --> 00:19:42,840
(Dog yelping)

178
00:19:47,029 --> 00:19:52,480
(Dog yelping)

179
00:19:57,114 --> 00:19:58,460
Hurry, we don't have much time!

180
00:20:38,179 --> 00:20:39,480
(Laughs)

181
00:20:40,209 --> 00:20:41,209
(Laughs)

182
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,080
(Laughs)

183
00:20:42,419 --> 00:20:43,500
(Laughs)

184
00:20:43,599 --> 00:20:45,640
(Laughs)

185
00:20:54,159 --> 00:20:55,460
(Laughs)

186
00:20:56,260 --> 00:20:57,260
Okay!

187
00:21:05,989 --> 00:21:07,900
Sigh... Look at the mess you've made.

188
00:21:08,469 --> 00:21:14,300
Grandpa is going to scold me.

189
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,200
(No audio)

190
00:21:24,629 --> 00:21:26,320
The other culprit must be Mokku.

191
00:21:26,524 --> 00:21:28,920
What would you have done if you started a forest fire?!

192
00:21:29,559 --> 00:21:32,520
We should just smash that mischievous little puppet to pieces!

193
00:21:32,975 --> 00:21:33,975
Yeah, that's right!

194
00:21:34,110 --> 00:21:39,080
Please, wait. It's my fault for not watching him closely enough. I'll make sure he never does anything like this again.

195
00:21:39,209 --> 00:21:42,460
Please, forgive him just this once for my sake. I'm begging you.

196
00:21:43,639 --> 00:21:46,460
Please forgive me!

197
00:21:50,694 --> 00:21:52,020
Just this once, old man.

198
00:21:52,594 --> 00:21:55,530
If he pulls a stunt like this again, we're smashing him to bits!

199
00:22:09,389 --> 00:22:11,200
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

200
00:22:12,979 --> 00:22:18,420
Having me around only makes you suffer, Grandpa. It's fine if I'm destroyed.

201
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:21,180
You fool!

202
00:22:30,469 --> 00:22:37,420
Mokku, you're a kind-hearted puppet. You saved Piko's baby, didn't you?

203
00:22:37,719 --> 00:22:42,680
You're a good boy. Mokku, you are Grandpa's treasure.

204
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:46,780
Grandpa!

205
00:22:56,659 --> 00:23:00,420
Thank you, Mokku. Mokku. I will never forget this for the rest of my life.

206
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:13,340
[[NO AUDIO]]

207
00:23:33,969 --> 00:23:39,760
Next time, learning of Mokku's wish to become human, Nora the stray cat plots something terrible.

208
00:23:40,795 --> 00:23:44,240
"If you gouge out a human's heart, you can become human."

209
00:23:45,075 --> 00:23:47,140
That is what Nora instills in Mokku.

210
00:23:48,865 --> 00:23:51,980
Caught targeting a young boy's heart,

211
00:23:52,344 --> 00:23:55,620
Mokku is nearly destroyed in retaliation by the boy's parents.

212
00:23:57,684 --> 00:24:00,220
Look forward to next week's Mokku of the Oak Tree!

